= Theory of mind — Simple =

'''Theory of mind''' is the ability to think about what other people or agents know, believe, want, feel, or intend.

You use it when you understand that someone else can believe something that is false, want something different from you, or act based on information you do not have.

Researchers often use '''false-belief tasks''' to study this ability in children.

But one false-belief test is not the whole of theory of mind. Language, memory, attention, and understanding the question can also affect the result.

AI systems can sometimes answer theory-of-mind-style questions, but passing a test does not prove that the system represents minds in the same way humans do.

